# An example of a pure commons project
proposer: "fiscalhost2"
name: "Heritage digitization for old palm-leaf collections, and pre British-era documents"
desc: """
  My mother expired recently, and her last wish was that many of the historical artifacts
  that we possess be well preserved, and be made available to everyone.  We've had
  discussions with preservationists, and found a home for these rare and precious
  artefacts in a museum/archive.

  Meanwhile, another friend of ours came up with the brilliant idea that we could get
  these digitized in very high quality, and make them available to the entire world
  using online portals, free for any kind of use, forever. That appealed to us, and
  we felt that this was the best way to honour the wishes of our late mother.

  We dug deeper, and found out that this isn't exactly a simple thing. A home scanner,
  or a scanner that you would find in offices, is cheap and fast.  But it's not high
  quality - in the \"heritage\" sense.  Heritage scanners are expensive and primarily
  deployed in museums and some libraries. We were able to find some services that offer
  careful handling and high quality digitization of these artifacts, but they charge
  a significant price per page. And we have more than fifty thousand pages to scan!

  We are able to cover the cost of transportation and some more logistics, and around
  40% of the digitization, but for the rest we are looking for some support from you.
  With your support, we can get the digitization done and upload the entire scanned
  copies under a public access license. Post that, the documents will be shifted to
  the archive for permanent storage, and access by researchers.
"""
funding_range:: 200000
campaign_url: "https://campaign.page/"
categories:: "short-term", "nascent"
licenses: "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
members::
  - ::
    uid: "uid7"
    fund_usage: """
      Heritage grade digitization of the royal family's private collection.
    """
